The attached image (Figure 5) demonstrates that Nano-11 significantly enhances the uptake of adsorbed antigens by bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs). Panel A, a flow cytometry dot plot, shows minimal uptake of soluble OVA or Nano-11 alone, but a substantial increase in the uptake of both Nano-11 and OVA when they are combined. Panel B, a histogram, further quantifies this, showing a marked shift to higher fluorescence intensity for FITC-labeled OVA when complexed with Nano-11, indicating enhanced antigen internalization by BMDCs. This supports Nano-11's role in improving antigen delivery to antigen-presenting cells.